{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/490830-the-hedge-could-it-be-a-host-to-a-large-community","id":490830,"title":"The Hedge: Could it be a host to a large community?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-24T12:59:09-07:00","id":490830,"title":"The Hedge: Could it be a host to a large community?","content":"Never have I played the Storyteller part(ok,once, and it was a disaster) so I don't know what I'm doing.I've been writing out a story for a campaign for...quite some time now. However, all this time I had neglected the mortal world. I had designed some people, places, and events but they were all in the Hedge. Court headquarters were large trods, as were some residences, historical conflicts were fought in it, etc. The only thing that I had focused on about the mortal world was the Spring Court's interactions with it (in my campaign, they're the ones with a lot of money as a result of being good at politics and marketing). I have a reason for this, though. Since I know my players will eventually find this thread, I'll stick to the basics: <br /> <br /> I\u2019m setting the story in British Columbia. The entire province is the setting, and it\u2019s all just one freehold. I\u2019ve written up a lot of backstory dating back to around the 1890\u2019s. The freehold of Prince George and its neighboring cities were suffering through a lot of abductions. Changelings would go missing all the time, and efforts to hunt down the Gentry proved to be wastes of time as even more people would go missing. To combat this, the four seasonal courts of Prince George had begun to negotiate with other freeholds to unite and form a larger one. Their goal was to create a community just for fae, in which involvement with mortals would be minimal. This way, the Lost would become more connected, creating a thicker line of defense against the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Creating a larger freehold meant fewer monarchs per square mile, and this was not a popular idea to some. Many monarchs abdicated without any resistance (for the greater good), while some clung to their power violently. Some freeholds had civil wars; the entire province was a giant clusterfuck for many decades before the Second World War. It was mainly the Winter Court (s) that had the greatest influence during this period of violence. One might assume it\u2019d be the Summer Court, since they are the militaristic faction. However, Winter courtiers would spy on their enemies and use the intelligence obtained to overpower their enemies.<br /> <br /> In the end, the province was united, with a huge power imbalance. The Winter Court ended up being the largest and most prosperous court. Their goal was achieved. They had created a society in the Hedge, with each court having its own trod headquarters. Changelings were no longer going missing so frequently. <br /> <br /> There's much more to what happens after that and before the events of the campaign, but I came here wondering if this is a good idea. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5775-periculum","name":"Periculum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T13:32:51-07:00","id":490885,"title":"","content":"I think that it is an in-universe terrible idea (as contact with humans is one of the thins that stop Changelings going fucking bugnuts) but a fantastic setting to show how horribly wrong it could go.<br /> <br /> Edit: Did you ever play Bioshock? This community sounds like a Hedge-based Rapture waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T13:44:10-07:00","id":490893,"title":"","content":"Considering the low (or simply absent ) clarity of its citizens, the freehold shouldn\u00b4t be so different from any goblin town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:25:36-07:00","id":490993,"title":"","content":"It would likely become a goblin town in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T19:14:34-07:00","id":491173,"title":"","content":"For a mundane solution, I am planning on running a werewolf game on Vancouver Island. And while setting up for it I looked up all the communities on it. And you'd be amazed how many towns exist that no one from outside that area has heard of. I imagine that would remain true for the rest of BC (Hell Canada even). Especially farther north, you could have a whole town full of Changelings (maybe a 50/50 or 75/25 split, or for a truly dangerous level 100% of the citizens) that barely anyone knows exists, if it's on the map and pays taxes it's even better.<br /> <br /> And if the Winter Court is in control you'd have a easy explanation of why such a settlement exists in the far north of BC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house 